==English==
===Verb===
{{en-verb|maxes out|maxing out|maxed out|maxed out}}

# {{intransitive}} To [[reach]] the [[limit]] of one's [[capability|capabilities]].
# {{intransitive}} To reach a [[maximum]] or a point at which no more [[growth]] or [[improvement]] is [[possible]].
# {{transitive}} To use (something) to the limit of its capabilities
#: ''I've spent all afternoon shopping and '''maxed out''' my credit card.''

====Usage notes====
This phrase is informal and should be avoided in written English.

